 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "nums is a non-empty list of n integers and k is a positive divisor of n. Randomness is injected so the result is reproducible: randomInts has exactly n - 1 entries, each in [0, 1e9]. Shuffle a copy of nums with Fisher-Yates: for i = n - 1 down to 1, take the next random value r and swap the elements at positions i and r mod (i + 1). Return k lists, where list s holds the shuffled elements at positions s * (n / k) through (s + 1) * (n / k) - 1.",
  "provenance": [
   {
    "repository": "gamma",
    "revision": null,
    "path": "projects/algorithm_solver/catalogue/authored/hack2hire-chunk17-a-20261028-v1/contracts.json",
